  "summary": "Does a cross-asset move during one region session predict the NEXT open of a currency that was closed while it moved? The only structurally defensible cross-asset LEAD (s16).",
  "research_window": "2015-01-01..2022-12-31 (research_only; 2023+ holdout untouched by this battery)",
  "primary_statistic": "OLS slope of target_ret ~ intercept + predictor_ret, one obs/day, one-sided p in the pre-registered sign. Intercept absorbs unconditional session drift (e.g. the h002 London-open effect), so the slope isolates the incremental predictor information.",
  "cross_check": "signed_return_test(sign*predictor_ret, target_ret) blocked by day, horizon_bars=1 (one non-overlapping obs/day).",
  "gate": "Benjamini-Hochberg FDR q=0.10 across the 15 tradeable cells. Bonferroni-over-cumulative (180+N) reported for context only.",
  "survivor_meaning": "A survivor is a CANDIDATE, not a green light. Research data (2015-2022) has been searched ~180 times, so this is exploratory. Confirmation: GOLD-based cells on fresh 2003-2014 data; all others via forward paper trading (equity/commodity CFDs only start ~2012, so no deep historical fresh slice exists).",
  "lookahead_control": "pair_lead pairs each predictor session only with a target session STARTING at or after the predictor ENDS (merge_asof forward). Verified by assertion at runtime and by tests/test_session_lead.py.",
  "overlap_control": "Exactly one observation per session-day, disjoint windows -> no serial overlap (s0.5 trap #1 does not apply).",
  "caveats": [
    "VIX (data from 2022 only), DXY (2017, and near-circular with the USD strength factor), and bond CFDs (2018) were excluded on data-depth grounds.",
    "B2/B3/E cells have ambiguous sign priors (EUR/GBP are neither clean risk nor haven currencies); they are included but expected weak.",
    "Even a survivor faces the same cost wall as everything else in this project; economic significance is a separate question from the slope test."
